  "note": "Genesis downloads each release program from url into genesis/programs/ and refuses any file whose sha256 is not the pin. A row with a mainnet object is read from mainnet instead: a program from its ProgramData, pinned by its executable_sha256 (the sha256 of the ELF without trailing zeros), and an account in accounts[], pinned by its data_sha256. loader, sha256 and bytes are what genesis seeds. upstream_upgrade_authority and the programdata fields record mainnet at mainnet_slot, for genesis/check-manifest.py's drift report. Ordering here is by address, for reading; it does not set the order genesis writes. A row with a part is seeded only on a network that turns the part on: ephemeral-rollup by svmd init --ephemeral-validator, vrf by --vrf-oracle.",
